A||||4||Dave85||Fuel pump replacement
Z||000000||Dave85||08-04-99||11:14 PM||||I have found an '88 Formula in near perfect shape really dirt cheap. They say that the fuel pump went out. When I turn on the ignition the pump does not run. Anyway, how hard of a fix is it? <br>
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||08-04-99||11:51 PM||||It's not too hard or too fun. There are 2 staps at the rear and front of the tank and a big plate in the center. You should empty the tank to make it lighter. You can by-pass the wiring in the pump plug to make it pump all the gas out of the supply hose(the bigger of the 2 going to the injectors) and into a can. Then remove all the bolts from the straps and the center plate. You may have to pull the tank down past the insulated water pipes. After it's on the ground you can tap the ring on the top that holds the pump in place, then the pump lifts right out. The ring spins to release the pump. 
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||08-04-99||11:54 PM||||I guess since the pump is not working you can't use it to pump out the gas. My guess is you are gonna get a bunch of gas on you :)
Z||000003||Shaun41178||08-05-99||01:34 AM||||DUDE check the fuel pump fuse first!!!!  If it is broken then of course the fuel pump wont' run.  When my fuel pump went bad it would still run but could not keep the pressure to keep the car running.  <p>Again check the fuse to see if it is broken.<p>If it is broken then you have found a great car for a even greater price.<p>Good luck.
Z||000004||DJRice||08-05-99||07:52 AM||||You should also check the Fuel pump relay..<p>Thats a much easier fix than removing the tank.
